          "question": "Who does guidance describe as a priority group for influenza vaccination?",
          "answer": "The guidance on influenza vaccination recommends routine annual vaccination for everyone aged 6 months and older, provided there are no contraindications. This approach is not limited to high-risk groups but encourages widespread vaccination to prevent influenza in the general population. According to the National immunization advisory committee and infectious diseases society guidance, the goal is to vaccinate by the end of October in the northern hemisphere to ensure protection during the typical flu season. \n\nI could not cover any specific high-risk groups mentioned separately in other documents, as the retrieved passage focused on the general recommendation for all individuals aged 6 months and older.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
